ecrosis along the veins  but  much later in infection then you will  see that the plants completely recover  from infection and the new leaves are  apparently healthy  so the first thing that we did when we  started  looking at this phenomenon is to see how  much virus is actually present in those  leaves at the different stage of  infection  and we expected that there would be less  virus in the recovered leaf because this  is what had been reported for other  nipple viruses  but to our surprise the level of viral  rna were maintained during the course of  infection and in fact there were very  high level of viral irony in the  recovered leaf as i'm showing you here  on this northern plot  so then the next question was okay  there's still a lot of viral ionia is  rna silencing active against tomato ring  spot virus in recovered leaf  so what we did to that is we compared  two types of plants plants that were  healthy or leaves that were recovered  from tomorrow's v infection  and we  injected those leaves  with  two types of constructs  one was  so in each case we had the green  fluorescent protein as a reported gene  and in the bottom comes to up here  where i show this little square in the  red those are tomato ring spot virus  sequence  so the idea is that if silencing is  already pre-induced against tomato ring  spot virus it should target this  construct and prevent its expression and  in fact this is what we saw if you look  on the bottom panels  on the right here you can see that in  healthy plants the green fluorescence  protein is expressed very well and we  see high level of fluorescence but it's  not expressed in tomato rigs but as far  as recovered leaves indicating that  financing against tomorrow's v is active  in doing sleeves  and we have a control where the the bit  of sensor  gene that we added is from a different  virus cucumber necrosis virus and in  this case the gfp protein is expressed  very well into  healthy and recovered leaf so this  indicated to us that rna silencing  specific to tamari tomato ring spot  virus was active in recovered leaves  another thing that we did is to look  whether small rnas were present and  especially those that were specific for  tomato ring spot virus so we use  northern blots again and we could show  that indeed there is small rna specific  for tomato ring spot virus active in  these leaves  so this tells us that  yes irony silencing is active but it's  not managing to bring down the  concentration of our lining  so something else is happening  um and i forgot to mention that all the  work i've uh presented before was the  beautiful work of uh  i'm going to go back to that side of  juan rafael and melanie walker and i'm  indicating the reference to the journal  at the end  at the bottom of the slide  at that point uh new student came in the  lab bachelor dev goshau  and he was interested in looking at the  molecular mechanism of this in more  detail and we took advantage of an  interesting phenomenon that  the  symptom recovery is actually dependent  on the growth temperature of the plants  and so you can see that plants grown at  27 degrees  will go through a phase of infection and  disease in inoculated leave and in  symptomatic leave but will eventually  recover from infection and if you look  at the picture of the plants on the  right sides at 20 dpi it's a reasonably  happy plant  the same virus infected on the same  batch of plant but let grown at 21  degrees you will see that the plants  really get very severely diseased and is  unable to recover from infection  so um what bashu dev did is to look at  what's happening in those leaves treated  at 21 degrees or 27 degrees and we  looked at  initial  leaves or leaves later in infection that  in 21 degrees were severely diseased or  in 27 degrees were recovered  and he first looked at the concentration  of viral rlrna and showed the same as  we had shown before  where the  concentration of rlrna was maintained in  rec